Executor gateway registration for the Herdr tools MCP server (N3.4 —
prepared, not installed).

What this is
------------
Every harness (Pi, Claude, Devin) reaches Herdr through the Executor MCP
gateway instead of a direct MCP registration. `herdr-mcp-integration.json`
holds the two payloads needed to register the local stdio Herdr MCP server on
the executor daemon, keyed by the exact executor tool path that consumes each.
Nothing in this directory has been registered anywhere; the daemon's own
registry (`provider:"file"`, behind the daemon API) is the only live store,
so there is no declarative file drop — prepared means payload plus runbook.

The registered env carries `HERDR_EXECUTOR_DELEGATED=1`: the gateway spawns
one server per connection with static env, so injected per-pane identity is
impossible and callers assert `{ paneId, projectRoot }` per call (the
`caller` argument on herdr_launch/herdr_run/herdr_status). The thin client
derives the D2a claim from a fresh `api snapshot` plus the caller assertion;
the daemon's verification is unchanged and remains the authority. Custody is
caller-asserted under the same-UID cooperative stance — strictly weaker than
environment-injected custody — acceptable because every gateway caller is a
Herdr-launched lane on this host.

Prerequisites for activation (all at the N5.3 cutover)
------------------------------------------------------
1. The daemon is installed and running: `systemctl --user enable --now
   herdr-tools-daemon` with `HERDR_SOCKET_PATH` in
   `~/.config/herdr-tools/daemon.env` (socket path must match the payload's
   `HERDR_SOCKET_PATH`).
2. The build is installed so
   `/home/gabriel/.pi/agent/extensions/herdr-tools/dist/src/mcp-server.js`
   exists at the path the payload's `args` names.
3. This tree is merged (the delegated `caller` field and the delegated
   startup gate must exist in the served build).

Pre-activation negative probe
-----------------------------
Before registering, prove nothing is live yet. From any executor-capable
harness (inside `executor_execute`):

    tools.executor.mcp.getServer({ slug: "herdr" })          -> not found
    tools.search({ namespace: "herdr", query: "status" })    -> no herdr tools

Activation — three executor calls at N5.3
-----------------------------------------
1. `tools.executor.mcp.addServer(herdr-mcp-integration.json["tools.executor.mcp.addServer"])`
   — registers the `herdr` slug (stdio, `spawnPerCall:false`: one shared
   stateless process, matching the thin client which holds nothing between
   calls).
2. `tools.executor.coreTools.connections.create(herdr-mcp-integration.json["tools.executor.coreTools.connections.create"])`
   — creates the `org`/`default` connection on the `herdr` integration.
3. `tools.executor.coreTools.connections.refresh(...)` — refreshes the
   connection so its tools appear.

Post-activation positive probe
------------------------------
    tools.executor.mcp.getServer({ slug: "herdr" })
        -> readback matches the payload (stdio, env trio, spawnPerCall:false)
    tools.search({ namespace: "herdr", query: "launch" })
        -> exactly herdr.org.default.herdr_{launch,run,status}
    tools.herdr.org.default.herdr_status({
        caller: { paneId: "<this pane>", projectRoot: "<canonical root>" } })
        -> well-formed reply, or bounded DAEMON_UNAVAILABLE if the daemon is down

Direct-registration removal (prepared diffs — do NOT apply early)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
`remove-direct-herdr-claude.diff` empties
`herdr-profiles/role-plugins/manager/mcp-servers.json` (the Claude manager
role plugin's direct stdio `herdr` registration).
`remove-direct-herdr-devin.diff` removes the `herdr` entry from
`~/.config/devin/mcp_config.json` (the `executor` entry stays — it is the
gateway itself).

Both diffs ride the N5.3 cutover alongside the skill landing: applying them
before the gateway is live breaks still-live managers' only Herdr reach.
Until cutover, live configs keep their direct registrations and this
directory changes nothing.
